## Usage: tasks/qemu-system/is-active --machine NAME
##
## Say whether the guest of the machine NAME has booted: whether its
## systemd has reached the target it boots to.
##
##   tasks/qemu-system/is-active --machine guest
##
## It fails while the guest takes no connection yet or still boots, so
## a workflow repeats it. A unit of the guest that failed does not fail
## it: a suite's own tests leave such units, and the guest still runs
## the next. It runs on the host and reaches the guest as systemctl
## does with --host.
. "$(dirname "$0")/../common/task"
: "${machine:?}"

transcript
systemctl --host "$machine" is-active default.target
